WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.480
Super Spike V-Ball Nintendo World Cup.

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:08.240
Bump, Set, Spike, Pass, Shoot, Score!

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:31.680
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every SKU released in North America.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:32.740
I'm Mike.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.000
I'm Sean.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:35.380
And I'm Joe.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:42.240
Guys, we had briefly covered in last week's episode that the reason for this existing

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:48.920
was the same reason as last week's episode, which was to sell Nintendo consoles in various

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:56.620
bundles. This one being, hey, we published two sports games that both have four-player compatibility.

00:00:56.620 --> 00:01:02.000
Why don't we just sell four controllers and an adapter for those four controllers and an

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.940
NES in this game and see if anybody will bite.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:11.520
And let's do it at the same time as we sell a different bundle that has an NES, two controllers,

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:16.800
a Zapper, and an NES Power Pad, which everybody wants, right?

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:17.800
Everybody wants a Power Pad.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:24.560
But since we covered that last episode, and there's really not much else to say there unless

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:28.880
this just, you know, maybe just real fast sound like a deal to you, which one's the better

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:31.220
deal? Definitely last week's, right?

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:37.980
I mean, this is great, but I mean, it's like a sport that is not very popular, like not,

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:41.820
you know, not like one of the main popular sports, which is volleyball.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.560
And then soccer, which is pretty popular worldwide.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:50.380
But it's also like, I don't know, I feel like not everyone's favorite soccer game or anything.

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:52.380
It's just like the other one is like Mario and Duck Hunt.

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:53.920
You know, it's like they're iconic.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:02:02.520
I'd say that even though they kind of force you to dispose of that last peripheral, like

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:05.060
it's really just being like, and take this too.

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:10.880
Even though you then have to throw that out and like deal with Garbage Day, it's still

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:15.160
better value. Or if you're, you know, in Joe's case, you could just use it as a towel.

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:17.040
Yes. Use a towel as it.

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:18.660
Yes. No, no.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:19.720
Or this time reverse it.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:21.140
Oh, just use it as your towel.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:24.480
Use a power pad as your towel. Because all my towels are in use for being power pads.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:26.000
So I need to use the power pad as a towel.

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:28.820
Yes. I agree.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:34.820
I think it's a no brainer that even regardless of whether the power pad that comes with it

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:39.500
works or not, the fact that you're getting Mario Brothers, Super Mario Brothers, and Duck

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:41.120
Hunt, and a working zapper.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:46.700
And all that other stuff is just like, it opens up more opportunity for you on the NES

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:52.640
as opposed to this one where I really feel like these were, these were fine games, Super

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:54.640
Spike V-Ball and Nintendo World Cup.

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:58.640
But I know I personally would not have ordered this one.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:00.180
I wouldn't have asked for it for Christmas.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:06.760
It would be like, to me, Joe, to your point, these are not the exciting sports I want.

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:08.260
I want a baseball game.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:09.240
I want a hockey game.

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:10.860
I would settle for a football game.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:14.500
And then eventually if I found out it was Tecmo Bowl, I'd be really happy that it was

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:17.780
a football game. But yeah, that's like where my head's at.

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:22.520
And that's kind of what I wanted this episode to be about because we are always talking about

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:28.860
since literally the very first episode, which was 10 Yard Fight, we have mentioned that like,

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:32.980
I don't know what it's going to take for a sports game to be on the essential games list.

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:40.020
And rather than say what we think an NES game that could be on the essential games list as a sports game is

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:46.940
or could be or set up rules for it, I just more or less wanted to explore sports video games in general

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:49.540
that we think are essential games.

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:55.620
Games that you, whether they were exposed to you at an early age for whatever console you had

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:58.200
and you were like, yep, I still think fondly of this game.

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:02.220
Or if it's actually like, yeah, it's still one of my favorite video games,

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:03.740
even though it's a sports game.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:08.860
That's kind of what I wanted this episode to be, just to maybe color some perspective

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:13.700
on why we don't vote these, historically we don't vote these NES games as essential.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.040
I mean, we have with one, right?

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:17.320
Yeah, sure.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:19.480
At least. I think maybe there were two, weren't there?

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:22.040
No, two. Yeah, there was Baseball Stars as well.

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:23.060
Yes, yes, okay.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:27.620
But yes, there is a higher bar for these games.

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:31.960
And so just thinking about it, a lot of sports games for me that I am,

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:42.300
fond of are mostly because I played them at a young age and they had the roster that I enjoyed as a kid.

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:44.740
The superstars I looked up to.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:48.560
And I don't think those are great criterias for a good video game.

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:59.340
And I'm sure if I played some of those today, I would actually prefer maybe some of the more like bare bones gameplay that's happening here on the NES than on those games.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:09.280
Because the early 3D era wasn't exactly, you know, the peak output for any video game genre.

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:14.120
I don't think anybody would say that the best baseball game lives on the N64.

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:22.700
Yeah, I think the real turning point was like the PS3 era.

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:27.380
I think that's when people started to see them as degrading in quality.

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:38.480
So I would say that PS2, Xbox, those were when most of the great sports games were coming out.

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:40.980
Yeah. And I'll be honest.

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:47.980
I think I might be not the best person for this experiment because I was not a big sports game person.

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:51.640
Both of my brothers, big, big into MLB and NHL.

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:53.540
And, you know, I definitely dabbled.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:06:02.920
But most traditional team sports games, I'm probably not going to vote on the essential games regardless because it's just not generally for me.

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:04.420
But I do have some thoughts.

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:14.940
We'll get into it. Yeah, well, I would actually like to start with you then, Joe, just to kind of get a baseline of when you think, you know, greatest sports games that you've played.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:18.100
Obviously, there's way more available than you've had access to.

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:21.800
But like what comes to mind as your great sports video games?

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:29.000
Well, so, you know, as a kid, it would always be like I'd only be playing these games if it was like my brother or one of my friends.

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:30.100
Like they just needed someone else.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.140
And I'm like, all right, fine.

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:34.440
I'll play, you know, NHL or I'll play MLB.

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:35.360
I mean, those are the big ones.

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:37.640
I never really played Madden much or anything like that.

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:43.300
But but those like are the ones that I would play here and there.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:52.320
I remember also playing a Ken Griffey game where you could play like on the kitchen table and you'd like the home run was like hitting it over the milk and stuff like that.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:53.840
That was kind of fun.

00:06:53.900 --> 00:07:00.340
But I think for me, it's more like if you want me to talk about standout sports games that I would call essential.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:01.580
They're not team sports games.

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:05.140
They're Tony Hawk's Pro Skater or SSX Tricky, things like that.

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:12.580
I mean, I spent tons of time in Tony Hawk and especially the first one when the remake came out more recently like that.

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:13.840
That game holds up.

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:19.580
And it is I think for me what it is, is that it's something that I can't do.

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:25.560
You know, I could get on a skateboard and go a couple feet, but like I cannot really do anything that's happening in that game.

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:35.460
And like obviously, if I'm playing an NHL game, I can't play hockey like the people in that game, but I could like still play amateur, you know, backyard hockey.

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:38.840
Whereas I just like can't even do anything on a skateboard.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:45.320
So it's like a little more wish fulfillment or a little more like amazing to me that I can like I think that's where the fun comes in.

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:51.280
Whereas like I can do all this stuff that like I'd have to work my whole life to be able to even come close to doing in reality.

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:54.120
And I totally count those as sports games.

00:07:54.260 --> 00:08:02.620
Like when I'm thinking about this, I would include ESPN NFL 2K5 as the same sports game as Mario Golf.

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:08.460
You know, like I don't achieving two different things, but they're definitely both sports video games.

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:16.400
Yeah, but like I think like there and I don't want to call them sub genres, but I think that they are like Tony Hawk.

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:29.260
Yes, skateboarding is a sport in a way, but it's not a sports game to me, nor is anything that Mario does.

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:41.740
If Mario got onto the gridiron and was like the quarterback of the Mushroom Kingdom mushrooms or something, then maybe.

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:44.140
But I don't know.

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:46.760
So there was a Mario baseball game.

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:50.620
Are you saying that that is falling on the line?

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:52.720
Yeah, I guess it depends.

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:55.600
I've never seen it. So maybe tennis.

00:08:55.940 --> 00:09:00.440
There was also a Mario soccer game. Like golf games are like, I guess those are sports games.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:05.460
I guess it's just whether or not you're considering it a team sport game or just sports games in general.

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:07.240
Like I feel like I get what you're saying.

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:11.860
I feel like the games that I normally think of when I think of sports games are team sports games.

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:14.060
Hockey, baseball, football, soccer.

00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:15.420
You know, things like that.

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:17.340
Yeah, I guess I can see it both ways.

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:18.580
It's just a different type of sport. Yeah.

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:30.240
What I'm thinking is that like on the NES, we're considering all these games as sports games, whether they take golf in the simulation realm or they try to be, you know, have fun with it.

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:37.660
Right. I don't know if we're calling Lunar Pool a sports game, but maybe we should look into that.

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:56.640
However, I guess that's what I'm saying, too, is like, you know, I totally understand that Mario Golf is not Tiger Woods PGA Tour, but they both, you know, are like serving a similar function that like I don't think people are playing Mario Golf strictly because they love Mario.

00:09:56.640 --> 00:09:59.900
Like you have to have some interest in golf, too.

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:33.940
Yeah. That like Dota or League of Legends.

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:38.260
Like these are video games with characters and abilities.

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:43.240
And it just so happens that people play them competitively.

00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:50.600
I don't know if I would say that that's a sport, but now we're getting into actual like linguistics and stuff.

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:56.680
Yeah. Right. I kind of want to like just for the heck of it workshop that line, like where did I draw that line?

00:10:56.680 --> 00:11:04.160
Because I agree with you that like League of Legends or something like definitely not a sport, even if it's an e-sport or if it's a competitive video game.

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:10.700
But like Rocket League, that does fall a little bit on like a line because it's like closer.

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:12.140
It's not a real sport.

00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:14.520
Yeah. But it's like trying to be like a sport.

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:17.540
You know what I mean? It's like a game about like a hybrid sport.

00:11:17.540 --> 00:11:29.720
But it is like you're trying to score a goal on another person, you know, like because then I wonder like if if there's there's the baseball game where you have like you can like turn into fire and charge the mound and stuff.

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:31.520
And like, is that a sport?

00:11:31.780 --> 00:11:33.060
Oh, it's like baseball. Yes.

00:11:33.220 --> 00:11:36.960
Yeah. Like it's baseball, but also there's like you have powers and stuff like that.

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:38.140
So it's like it's weird.

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:42.140
I don't know exactly where it's like very fluid because I don't know exactly where I would draw the line.

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:43.680
Like, no, that's just strictly an e-sport.

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:45.620
And this is a sports game.

00:11:45.620 --> 00:11:52.020
But like, yeah, do we think it has to be based on an actual real life sport or can there be a fictional sport?

00:11:52.180 --> 00:11:54.160
Is Quidditch World Cup a sports game?

00:11:54.540 --> 00:12:04.860
Or like, you know, that's what I was going to say is like, you know, I think I draw the line on it not being a real sport because, Joe, even your that game that we loved that's like the kickball game.

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:06.860
Oh, yeah. Kung fu kickball.

00:12:08.300 --> 00:12:10.020
Like, that's not a sports game, right?

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:13.620
Yeah. I mean, I wouldn't think so until now that you've challenged me on that.

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:17.220
I'm like, well, I guess based on what I just said, it would have to be.

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:21.020
So I don't know. It can't be because then like Smash Brothers becomes a sports game.

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:26.280
Like, you know, I would even go as far as to say like Gran Turismo games aren't sports games.

00:12:26.420 --> 00:12:31.360
Those are racing games and they're closer to like need for speed than they are to NFL Blitz.

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:33.960
Yeah. I mean, I guess the yeah.

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:36.000
And this is a loose line, even as I'm thinking of it.

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:46.240
But like the difference between like Smash Brothers and Kung Fu kickball is that Kung Fu kickball is two people with a soccer ball trying to quote unquote score a goal on each other.

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:53.920
Whereas which is like very much seems like it's taken mostly from soccer with like a bunch of other stuff added to it.

00:12:53.920 --> 00:13:00.120
Whereas Super Smash Brothers is like here are these video game characters doing the things they do in their video games and they're all fighting each other.

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:08.220
I propose that the that we go with the idea that the sport has to exist in real life for it to be a sports game.

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:11.900
So NASCAR, those are sports games.

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:13.320
Motorsport, I guess, counts.

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:24.280
And NFL Blitz is a sports game, even though they don't they they may like, you know, turn on fire or whatever happens.

00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:25.500
It's been a while.

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:27.760
They do. They do turn on fire.

00:13:28.180 --> 00:13:29.420
Turn on fire.

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:34.560
But it's still based on football.

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:43.020
And but I don't think that like Rocket League, even though it's based on soccer, you are not a car in soccer.

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:45.420
So I accept your proposal.

00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:48.080
I think Joe gave us a good tangent there.

00:13:48.240 --> 00:14:01.320
And now we can go back to the actual question and maybe get an answer from Sean this time around on like, Sean, just some greatest of all time sports video games that are captured in your mind.

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:09.920
Yeah. In order, I'll say NBA Jam when I was truly little.

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:12.600
Got to be on got to be on the list.

00:14:12.760 --> 00:14:17.460
Yeah. So that would be when I had the Super NES played that a lot.

00:14:20.100 --> 00:14:24.060
Then it was probably like I think it was NASCAR 98, though.

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:28.620
I never really like treat treated it as a racing game.

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:44.020
Like, I don't think I ever completed a race like there was there was a code that you could input that gave you a basically like a BB gun that you could shoot like spheres out of the front of your car.

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:49.560
And you basically just turned it into like twisted metal on a racetrack kind of.

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:53.600
So we me and my stepbrother would would do that.

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:56.720
Then Madden 08.

00:14:57.140 --> 00:15:06.520
I probably played a franchise for 15, 16 in game years and move some teams around.

00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:08.600
It was really funny. I had a team in Mexico City.

00:15:08.740 --> 00:15:10.140
I had a team in Calgary.

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:17.320
Then I think those are the three like formative sports games.

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:24.200
Everything since that PS2 Xbox era has just been kind of whatever.

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:27.080
I think it's a I think it's a solid draft.

00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:32.140
And, you know, working off of what we're you know, what is a sports game?

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:43.180
What isn't and iconic ones I tend to pick is like my favorite sports games, even even though there are actual simulation ones like pick any year of the show, probably.

00:15:43.180 --> 00:15:50.660
And I think it's, you know, an amazing experience or we were talking about and we have mentioned so many times NFL 2K5.

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:55.860
That's the ESPN one where you can also like build a house or an apartment.

00:15:56.040 --> 00:15:57.560
I forget. You can decorate a crib.

00:15:58.120 --> 00:15:59.580
Yeah. Oh, yeah. Decorate the house.

00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:03.560
Sure. But like, you know, you're doing that in addition to playing football.

00:16:04.140 --> 00:16:17.120
The same thing with was MVP baseball 2005 where you can just like set the price on concessions, but also be the batters and play the game at the same time as running the franchise.

00:16:17.340 --> 00:16:18.580
All those things are fun.

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:29.800
But I think the best sports video games in my head, the ones that like I go back to and keep playing are the ones that make the sport more exciting than real life.

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:35.580
Like the Sims stuff does a great job of making me feel like I'm in the shoe of those athletes.

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:36.660
But it doesn't.

00:16:36.820 --> 00:16:38.360
Just one shoe. Yeah.

00:16:38.380 --> 00:16:39.300
I can't wear both shoes.

00:16:39.440 --> 00:16:42.280
There's just not going to pretend to be in both of Josh Allen's shoes.

00:16:42.460 --> 00:16:44.180
Right. But maybe one shoe.

00:16:44.380 --> 00:16:45.480
Maybe I'm cleaning it for him.

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:48.320
Just one shoe still doesn't.

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:52.840
These games, though, like, you know, I'm going to throw out some crazy ones.

00:16:52.940 --> 00:16:57.500
Okay. But like Wii Sports is a sports game.

00:16:57.780 --> 00:17:05.740
It is a sports game. And I think it's one that like I will go back to forever, especially with other people.

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:11.700
Like it was the introduction to the Wii motion controls and it absolutely nailed it.

00:17:11.780 --> 00:17:13.440
And it makes those games fun.

00:17:13.660 --> 00:17:16.060
It makes bowling somehow more fun than bowling.

00:17:16.340 --> 00:17:23.200
Not true. When you go bowling with someone who just can't throw the ball, right?

00:17:23.260 --> 00:17:24.600
So they're just going to keep getting gutters.

00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:29.720
They're just going to like no matter what they do, it gets halfway down there and then they just like lose momentum.

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:31.760
And that sucks for them.

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:32.860
And that's not fun for you.

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:37.140
And now you're just sitting there with some expensive beers and a pretty expensive pair of rental shoes.

00:17:37.420 --> 00:17:38.480
And it's just not working out.

00:17:38.480 --> 00:17:42.260
You get two lanes and put gutters, gutter bumpers on one.

00:17:42.460 --> 00:17:45.920
Come on. It makes the other person feel very self-conscious.

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:54.660
I'll say I've recently, my dad's having some hip surgery and he needed me to take over for him for this season in his bowling league.

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:58.240
And I've been bowling and I'm like, wow, bowling is great.

00:17:58.540 --> 00:18:00.340
I didn't know you bowled.

00:18:00.620 --> 00:18:01.700
I don't.

00:18:01.960 --> 00:18:06.080
I've been bowling for like the last, like once a month for the past like five months now.

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:08.620
And I'm like, yeah, this is like really fun.

00:18:09.180 --> 00:18:11.920
So I don't know. I have to Wii bowl again and compare.

00:18:12.740 --> 00:18:15.500
I guess what I'm saying is like I recently bowled like a 194.

00:18:16.020 --> 00:18:17.400
So like I'm not, I'm pretty good.

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:20.140
I'm not the greatest of all time by no means.

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:21.440
But like I'm pretty good at bowling.

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:23.780
I'm not disputing that the experience is fun.

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:26.920
I'm saying I think Wii bowling captures it completely differently.

00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:32.100
I don't, I think like that's my point about the games I'm going to list is like we were talking about NFL Blitz.

00:18:32.100 --> 00:18:36.000
It's like, yeah, I'm glad that people don't turn on fire in real life.

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:39.860
But it's such a fun phrase, Sean.

00:18:40.460 --> 00:18:43.840
But I'm, but I'm so excited when that happens in this game.

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:49.520
I'm so excited when like after the play is over, I just tackle the opponent and I'm just like, yeah, screw you.

00:18:49.700 --> 00:18:51.620
You know, like the fact you're allowed to do that.

00:18:51.780 --> 00:18:53.200
I would get in trouble for that in Madden.

00:18:53.280 --> 00:18:54.220
You would get in trouble.

00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:56.620
Or they just don't let you do it actually.

00:18:57.700 --> 00:18:59.460
Those are the games I keep looking at.

00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:03.140
But even just the ones that like gamify the sport.

00:19:03.340 --> 00:19:07.780
Like Mike Tyson, we talk about how that's more of a rhythm game than a boxing game.

00:19:08.280 --> 00:19:14.480
It manages to take, it manages to think about being a video game first and then working in the sports element.

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:17.740
And I think that's what I like about even backyard baseball.

00:19:17.740 --> 00:19:29.220
It's like such a feel good, earnest take on baseball, even though it uses like real MLB stars and puts them as kids.

00:19:29.440 --> 00:19:32.400
And the rules are like slightly adjusted and everything.

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:33.420
It makes it this way.

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:36.840
It's a, it's really just like a fun experience first.

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:40.300
And then you're like, oh yeah, but this is totally a baseball game.

00:19:40.560 --> 00:19:41.760
Yeah, I get it.

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:45.160
I think that there's definitely like a D mark.

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:48.240
I mean like, yeah, I guess there already is like, is it sim or is it arcade?

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:51.760
These are all arcade versions of sports.

00:19:52.140 --> 00:19:56.960
So that definitely is still valid though.

00:19:57.460 --> 00:20:08.220
And it's fun to like, it's fun to play the latest NHL, but it's probably more fun to actually feel like I have any sense of what I'm doing when I'm playing NHL 94.

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:20.580
Like there's just too much, there's too much to going on in, in the sim games now where I feel like, man, can I just, and thankfully we can, can we just turn on NHL 94 controls on these things and play them?

00:20:20.680 --> 00:20:23.720
And they, they do let you do that, which is very nice.

00:20:23.720 --> 00:20:39.340
Um, and I think that that's true of like every NBA game should also have like an NBA jam mode associated with it rather than like the timing systems and, and having to understand proper defense and stuff like that.

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:41.540
Like some people just want to have a quick pickup game.

00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:42.400
Um, well, okay.

00:20:42.420 --> 00:20:52.100
So I don't know if like not knowing how to play basketball is, but I never felt like I needed to know how to play basketball when I was playing NBA jam.

00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:53.900
It was just fun two on two, you know?

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:55.960
Yeah. Well, you need to know the rules of basketball.

00:20:56.260 --> 00:20:58.340
You don't need to know how to like shoot.

00:20:58.380 --> 00:21:00.120
Yeah. And I think that's what I'm advocating for.

00:21:00.220 --> 00:21:03.080
Right. It's like, I don't want to have to know defensive formations.

00:21:04.260 --> 00:21:11.920
Sure. Then yeah, I guess definitely play jam instead of, uh, whatever the, what is it?

00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:12.940
What's the EA one?

00:21:13.240 --> 00:21:15.140
Just, oh, it's just, it's just NBA.

00:21:15.260 --> 00:21:16.460
Isn't it just 2K? Yeah.

00:21:17.100 --> 00:21:18.160
It's just 2K.

00:21:19.420 --> 00:21:20.720
Wait, 2K is EA?

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:22.020
I thought 2K was like a competitor. No, no, no, no.

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:27.300
I forgot that EA hasn't, I think they took a few years off of NBA.

00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:29.540
Oh, I see. So it's just been 2K for a while.

00:21:29.800 --> 00:21:30.740
Yeah. Oh.

00:21:31.920 --> 00:21:34.240
Well, just certainly back to the Wii Sports thing.

00:21:34.240 --> 00:21:38.440
I wanted to throw a quick shout out to a game that probably nobody listening to this

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:43.720
has played because I don't think it was very popular, uh, which is the PlayStation Move

00:21:43.720 --> 00:21:48.620
Sports Champions, which I do think was like actually pretty amazing.

00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:50.160
It's just every who needed it.

00:21:50.260 --> 00:21:55.540
Everyone already had a Wii and nobody uses their PlayStation to be a Wii.

00:21:55.700 --> 00:22:02.220
But like that had like, it was like Wii Sports, but with, it was like beach volleyball,

00:22:02.480 --> 00:22:05.480
bocce. There was like a gladiator duel.

00:22:05.960 --> 00:22:07.700
And then, uh, oh, frisbee golf.

00:22:07.980 --> 00:22:09.100
And I think ping pong.

00:22:09.600 --> 00:22:14.420
And like, I mean, you know, objectively, much better controls than the Wii.

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:16.320
Ooh. Wow. Objective.

00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:18.020
I like. Yeah.

00:22:18.100 --> 00:22:23.360
Because nobody bought like a PlayStation Move, but my friends and I, one time we all pooled

00:22:23.360 --> 00:22:27.940
our tickets together at Dave and Buster's and got a PlayStation Move and this game.

00:22:28.460 --> 00:22:30.820
And then we would like split it five ways.

00:22:30.980 --> 00:22:32.940
Like every couple months we'd give it to the next person.

00:22:33.080 --> 00:22:35.380
And I think we all got like one turn with it before it was lost.

00:22:35.680 --> 00:22:36.800
But it was great.

00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:38.220
Lost. Quote unquote.

00:22:39.060 --> 00:22:39.920
Yeah. I'm pretty sure.

00:22:40.240 --> 00:22:42.980
You guys might be the first one to ever redeem anything at Dave and Buster's.

00:22:44.300 --> 00:22:46.380
Well, we had to pool all of our tickets.

00:22:46.580 --> 00:22:51.140
And I, I pretty sure one of my friends whose name I won't name sold it without any, without

00:22:51.140 --> 00:22:53.540
the permission of the rest of us and pocketed the money.

00:22:54.100 --> 00:22:56.940
Wow. But you're pretty sure you're, you're, yeah.

00:22:57.020 --> 00:22:58.000
You haven't confirmed that.

00:22:58.520 --> 00:22:59.620
No, it's confirmed.

00:23:02.860 --> 00:23:04.580
Wow. Thanks for the fast closure.

00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:07.780
Yeah. We took care of it.

00:23:08.380 --> 00:23:09.900
Yeah. Good. As you should.

00:23:10.160 --> 00:23:11.380
I just want to make it clear.

00:23:11.380 --> 00:23:13.920
I'm not against the existence of SIM games.

00:23:14.300 --> 00:23:17.140
I, I have, I dabble in them pretty often.

00:23:17.140 --> 00:23:22.400
I just think the more fun experience gameplay wise always comes from the ones that add that

00:23:22.400 --> 00:23:23.320
video game twist.

00:23:23.320 --> 00:23:29.260
I do appreciate being able to understand just how hard it is to hit a baseball in real life

00:23:29.260 --> 00:23:36.060
when I play MLB the show on the actual SIM modes, because once you see what 102 mile per

00:23:36.060 --> 00:23:41.340
hour up and in fastball looks like, you'll stop booing your favorite players and just resign

00:23:41.340 --> 00:23:43.500
yourself to the fact that you couldn't hit that ball if you tried.

00:23:45.360 --> 00:23:50.680
Well, even then it's like, you know, you're, you're, you're, even SIM games are super simplified

00:23:50.680 --> 00:23:58.120
and being good at Madden, especially, it does not mean that you would make a good coach or

00:23:58.120 --> 00:23:59.220
anything like that.

00:24:00.080 --> 00:24:02.520
I was pissed to find out being good at Guitar Hero.

00:24:02.520 --> 00:24:04.280
What did it mean? I was good at the real guitar.

00:24:06.140 --> 00:24:08.880
Didn't they eventually make one that was supposed to like teach you guitar?

00:24:08.880 --> 00:24:10.620
Rocksmith, right?

00:24:11.140 --> 00:24:12.620
Yes. Yeah.

00:24:12.620 --> 00:24:19.020
They do that for baseball. Rocksmith is the one where you use an actual guitar and then, but like, I think the stepping

00:24:19.020 --> 00:24:28.900
stone there would be Rock Band, which instead of having five buttons had like the whole fretboard

00:24:28.900 --> 00:24:29.760
was buttons.

00:24:31.540 --> 00:24:32.700
That didn't happen.

00:24:33.060 --> 00:24:36.340
That happened. That did not happen with Rock Band.

00:24:36.560 --> 00:24:39.260
The whole fretboard being, being buttons.

00:24:39.820 --> 00:24:42.380
Yeah. It was just, it was still just five buttons.

00:24:42.820 --> 00:24:47.020
Well, there was a pro controller or something that my friend had.

00:24:47.020 --> 00:24:48.500
Oh, okay. Well, that might've happened.

00:24:48.600 --> 00:24:52.740
Yeah. But then they also charted all those, they charted all those songs again?

00:24:53.180 --> 00:24:54.460
I'm almost positive.

00:24:55.080 --> 00:24:58.080
Now you're making me doubt myself, but I'm almost positive.

00:24:59.260 --> 00:25:00.760
I'm not trying to be like a jerk.

00:25:00.980 --> 00:25:03.500
I'm just waiting with bated breath because you are both so confident.

00:25:03.640 --> 00:25:05.180
I'm like, man, one of them's gotta be wrong.

00:25:06.580 --> 00:25:10.940
So I'm looking at it and the Rock Band Pro Guitar Controller is a real thing.

00:25:11.140 --> 00:25:14.140
17 fret, 102 button peripheral.

00:25:14.900 --> 00:25:21.880
But I just, I guess like, how the heck do they, but how do they rechart those songs for

00:25:21.880 --> 00:25:23.000
all those frets? It's like.

00:25:23.100 --> 00:25:25.720
They just do it. But they were so simplified.

00:25:25.720 --> 00:25:28.420
They turned every note in the game into just five buttons.

00:25:31.080 --> 00:25:32.100
They did it again.

00:25:32.220 --> 00:25:36.940
But that sounds awesome. But I wouldn't be able to do this anyway, because to my point, being good at five buttons

00:25:36.940 --> 00:25:38.120
doesn't make you good at 102.

00:25:38.760 --> 00:25:42.420
But also being good at 102 buttons doesn't make you good at guitar.

00:25:42.700 --> 00:25:45.680
So it's also just another step.

00:25:46.020 --> 00:25:48.280
I love the term being good at buttons.

00:25:49.580 --> 00:25:52.600
Like, this is a good way to describe like being a good video gamer.

00:25:53.080 --> 00:25:54.260
There's some good buttons.

00:25:54.580 --> 00:25:56.240
That is basically what games are.

00:25:56.900 --> 00:26:00.720
Don't you ever see those Nike hype videos where they show like LeBron James like pushing

00:26:00.720 --> 00:26:02.940
buttons really fast for his reaction times?

00:26:03.040 --> 00:26:04.140
And like, he's in the zone, right?

00:26:04.200 --> 00:26:06.740
And it's like, that's what it means to be really good at buttons.

00:26:08.160 --> 00:26:10.560
True. I don't know this commercial.

00:26:11.200 --> 00:26:14.940
Well, the commercial I'm referencing is probably way off the air by now.

00:26:15.140 --> 00:26:20.200
But, you know, there's always that like, you know, athlete in a training room kind of

00:26:20.200 --> 00:26:21.760
thing. And they're at the top of their game.

00:26:21.760 --> 00:26:26.360
But we can't show them in the game because we don't own the express written consent of

00:26:26.360 --> 00:26:27.820
the NBA. That's true.

00:26:28.620 --> 00:26:34.980
So they have to wear a generic, generic red jersey with just their number on the back.

00:26:35.100 --> 00:26:36.420
Just the Nike switch on it.

00:26:36.420 --> 00:26:37.440
Yeah. All right.

00:26:37.520 --> 00:26:43.420
So now moving away from the question of great, great sports games.

00:26:43.540 --> 00:26:46.780
Hopefully we came to some kind of conclusion there.

00:26:47.740 --> 00:26:51.520
What is the what is the opposite of that?

00:26:51.700 --> 00:26:58.300
What is like the the game that you played that turned you off the sport completely or

00:26:58.300 --> 00:27:05.500
made you like so frustrated that you gave up on like the series or franchise or sport?

00:27:05.500 --> 00:27:07.780
Hmm. That is a good question.

00:27:08.180 --> 00:27:13.060
And it doesn't even have to be one of the, you know, one of the core for sports.

00:27:13.160 --> 00:27:14.700
Like it doesn't have to be a baseball game.

00:27:14.840 --> 00:27:18.080
It could be a snowboarding game that was like, you know what?

00:27:18.160 --> 00:27:19.260
I'm done with snowboarding games.

00:27:21.180 --> 00:27:23.780
You know what? That might be that might be.

00:27:24.620 --> 00:27:25.640
No, no.

00:27:25.640 --> 00:27:30.660
I remember I rented a surfing game and it was it was really dumb.

00:27:32.040 --> 00:27:33.860
Oh, wait, maybe that was wakeboarding.

00:27:34.220 --> 00:27:36.820
I don't know. The water water sports are hard.

00:27:37.000 --> 00:27:40.120
I think it's just hard to make a good video game for a water sport.

00:27:42.480 --> 00:27:45.820
Like the one wakeboarding game.

00:27:46.080 --> 00:27:49.140
There was only one way to really do anything.

00:27:49.280 --> 00:27:51.100
Have you ever played this wakeboarding game?

00:27:52.260 --> 00:27:54.720
I'm trying to think of a wakeboarding video game.

00:27:54.960 --> 00:27:57.600
Yeah, I think there was wakeboarding in Wii Sports Resort.

00:27:58.460 --> 00:28:01.060
Was there? There's like a wakeboarding arcade game.

00:28:01.220 --> 00:28:02.200
I always remembered seeing.

00:28:02.880 --> 00:28:04.500
Wii Sports Resort, Sean.

00:28:04.740 --> 00:28:06.620
Not the. Oh, I see.

00:28:07.300 --> 00:28:08.300
That would be funny.

00:28:08.440 --> 00:28:11.260
They were like, yeah, we got bowling, baseball, boxing and wakeboarding.

00:28:13.180 --> 00:28:16.540
Yes. Wakeboarding unleashed with Sean Murray.

00:28:17.560 --> 00:28:19.660
Oh, it's even had a guy's name attached.

00:28:19.660 --> 00:28:21.740
Yeah. Never.

00:28:22.000 --> 00:28:33.000
Was never a big fan of the BMX games that tried to like riff off of basically any extreme sports game that wasn't Tony Hawk was pretty lame.

00:28:34.520 --> 00:28:39.520
I did. Well, I did play a cricket game once and that was that was fun because I couldn't understand any of it.

00:28:39.520 --> 00:28:40.880
But OK.

00:28:41.560 --> 00:28:50.020
But yeah, there's never been like a really terrible sports game that I was never watched the sport again because of it.

00:28:50.260 --> 00:28:51.920
Yeah, I'm digging for an answer here.

00:28:52.020 --> 00:28:57.340
I'm not sure. Yeah, there definitely wouldn't have been one where I'm like, oh, this is this is what turned me off of this whole sport.

00:28:57.340 --> 00:29:01.020
But like in the real world, I think just in general, I think just playing.

00:29:01.140 --> 00:29:04.560
I mean, honestly, I think part of the reason I'm not going to have a specific answer for you.

00:29:04.640 --> 00:29:14.060
But what like part of the reason that I don't like sports games that much might harken back to like when I was a little kid and my older brother really likes sports games.

00:29:14.060 --> 00:29:15.240
And I wanted to play Mario.

00:29:15.580 --> 00:29:22.460
We'd have to like play, you know, we'd have to play a game of Blades of Steel first before I before we could play Mario.

00:29:22.680 --> 00:29:23.580
It was like the deal we'd make.

00:29:23.700 --> 00:29:27.240
So that made me maybe just be like, oh, man, like this was feels more like a chore to me.

00:29:27.360 --> 00:29:29.360
And I might have maybe that ingrained itself in me.

00:29:29.460 --> 00:29:30.960
But like I like Blades of Steel now.

00:29:31.120 --> 00:29:35.960
But back then, you know, I'd always be like, let's get through Blades of Steel so we can play Super Mario Brothers 3.

00:29:35.960 --> 00:29:47.080
And I don't even think it has to be a bad game necessarily, because my example would be Dirt 5, which was free on Game Pass when I had Game Pass.

00:29:47.240 --> 00:29:49.640
And I was excited about it.

00:29:49.800 --> 00:29:51.360
Rally game. Let me check it out.

00:29:51.740 --> 00:29:55.680
And it was a mixture of like too realistic for me.

00:29:55.880 --> 00:30:01.480
But also like I couldn't grasp the concept of like this kind of racing.

00:30:01.480 --> 00:30:08.600
Like I just wasn't the fact that like the you have to like wear the headphones and the your coach, I guess.

00:30:08.720 --> 00:30:12.640
I don't know what they refer to that person who tells you when the turns are coming up.

00:30:12.760 --> 00:30:16.420
But like they're shouting that stuff in your ears and you have to anticipate it.

00:30:16.520 --> 00:30:18.900
And you're driving in the car and there's mud everywhere.

00:30:18.900 --> 00:30:21.820
And I was like, this is incredibly impressive.

00:30:21.820 --> 00:30:23.380
I can't do any of it.

00:30:23.580 --> 00:30:25.500
I can't drive this car.

00:30:25.960 --> 00:30:28.820
And it like pretty much turned me off rally games in general.

00:30:28.820 --> 00:30:32.340
I've tried a few other ones for two to three minutes.

00:30:32.340 --> 00:30:35.560
And I realize it's every time I can't drive these cars.

00:30:36.340 --> 00:30:43.760
Now, has that caused you to not be interested in rally as a sport in general or?

00:30:44.040 --> 00:30:46.700
No, I want to watch rally stuff in real life.

00:30:47.040 --> 00:30:48.080
Yeah, just the games.

00:30:48.160 --> 00:30:51.680
I just know now that I'm not good at them and it's not worth pursuing.

00:30:51.680 --> 00:30:56.840
But I would want to watch rally for the same reason I want to watch the free solo guy climb buildings.

00:30:56.840 --> 00:30:59.380
You know, I'm hoping to see something really cool happen.

00:31:00.520 --> 00:31:01.820
Something really cool.

00:31:02.020 --> 00:31:04.820
Cool, huh? Yeah, something really cool happened.

00:31:06.460 --> 00:31:08.200
Something you don't see every day.

00:31:11.820 --> 00:31:22.920
And I mean, there's also the, as you could tell from my attitude towards them, the realization that I have no idea how to coach a hockey team.

00:31:23.540 --> 00:31:28.060
That like, you know, the NHL games kind of exposed me to being like a phony.

00:31:28.680 --> 00:31:30.820
Whereas like baseball, I feel like I have an idea.

00:31:31.580 --> 00:31:39.840
You know, like when I play baseball games, I feel like I'm in control and I can manage the team and I can make the plays and I can call the plays.

00:31:39.840 --> 00:31:46.540
Because the NHL was, the NHL games were like an eye opener where I was like, I guess I really don't know anything other besides offsides and icing.

00:31:47.520 --> 00:31:49.520
I'm not even talking about from like a rules perspective.

00:31:49.520 --> 00:31:51.820
I'm just talking about like a strategy perspective.

00:31:52.160 --> 00:31:58.640
Like, I guess I really don't understand like skating formations and line changes and shit like that.

00:31:58.800 --> 00:32:01.200
Like, it just happens and we're lucky to see it.

00:32:01.200 --> 00:32:14.640
My problem with NHL was always just that like the, the, the, when you change the difficulty, like pro was just like, you can just score anytime you put the puck towards the net.

00:32:14.680 --> 00:32:21.960
And then all star or whatever the equivalent is, every goalie, like would just read your inputs.

00:32:21.960 --> 00:32:30.200
So I could never find that middle ground where like I'd get realistic scores because it's not fun to win seven to nothing or seven to two or whatever.

00:32:30.200 --> 00:32:45.320
So I think you've touched into something there, Sean, because that is how I feel about a lot of sports games in that N64 PS1 era as well, where once you figure these games out, it's very easy to just win ridiculous games.

00:32:45.480 --> 00:32:48.200
Like your baseball games can be like 19 nothing.

00:32:48.440 --> 00:32:52.800
And it's like, you know, that has happened, but it doesn't happen every single time you play.

00:32:53.200 --> 00:32:57.760
And yet that's what I was saying at the beginning is like, that's some of the stuff that like the formative games.

00:32:57.760 --> 00:33:02.740
Like when I think about Wayne Gretzky's 3D hockey or MLB featuring Ken Griffey Jr.

00:33:03.040 --> 00:33:07.260
Like those are two N64 games that I loved playing as a kid.

00:33:07.360 --> 00:33:15.580
And I, you know, I had kid like motor reflexes, so I wasn't winning crazy games or anything, but I was having so much fun.

00:33:15.780 --> 00:33:21.100
But on revisit, like those games aren't even close to the greatest sports games of all time.

00:33:21.100 --> 00:33:22.400
They were just like for me.

00:33:22.560 --> 00:33:28.520
And now I remember the sounds and the music and the rosters more than anything else.

00:33:28.520 --> 00:33:42.160
Yeah, I feel especially in that area, like with PlayStation 1, at least for me, you just you can't take your eyes off of the how like choppy it is.

00:33:42.280 --> 00:33:48.200
And it just doesn't feel this doesn't feel right anymore because you're trained on more modern games.

00:33:48.200 --> 00:34:01.040
And I think like, you know, with with a video game, like with an action game or like an adventure game that that might not be as as big of a deal because like the game is the game.

00:34:01.240 --> 00:34:02.840
